# Use skills when implementing

Whenever you implement, change, or refactor something in this project, **go through the relevant skills in `.agents/skills/` first** and follow them so best practices stay intact.

- Before writing code, identify which installed skills apply to the task (framework, routing, caching, data fetching, UI, tooling, etc.).
- Read those skills' `SKILL.md` (and linked references when needed) and apply their guidance.
- Prefer the skill's recommended patterns over improvising an equivalent approach.
- If a skill conflicts with an explicit user instruction, ask before proceeding.
- After implementing, quickly check that the change still matches the skill's constraints and recommended patterns.

```text
❌ BAD: Jump straight into coding a Next.js feature without reading applicable skills
✅ GOOD: Scan .agents/skills, read the matching SKILL.md files, then implement accordingly
```
